==Battleground==
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[CyberFace]] spawns as the boss.
**50 [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 2~6 seconds<sup>60f~180f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is like a puzzle, simple and quick, with the difficulty laying in knowing how to "solve" it.

By far the easiest method to beat this is spawning [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catornado]] (optionally with a [[Critical Hit|Critical]] chance up combo), as one Critical from even a mid-level Catornado is capable of killing the CyberFace. As a matter of fact, nearly any [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]] is able to instantly kill CyberFace provided their Crit ability activates; the only one that can't at level 30 is [[Million-Dollar Cat (Special Cat)|Million-Dollar Cat]], who has to deal two hits if below level 46.

If you don't have Catornado, the following may work: summon an ideally fast cat ([[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]>[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]]>[[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cow Cat]]>[[Cow Cat (Normal Cat)|Cow Cat]]); once this unit dies and CyberFace advances, intercept it with a meatshield while close to the base and follow by summoning as many Critical Hitters you own once CyberFace's next wave passes your base, or just one Critical Hitter with 100% chance. If the Critical Hitter has 100% Crit chance and a fast enough attack ([[Sunny Neneko (Super Rare Cat)|Sunny Neneko]], Million-Dollar Cat), you may use this unit to intercept CyberFace directly, instead of using a meatshield. The leftover spaces in your army can be used for either a failsafe measure or Combos to speed up the process or make success more likely.

Of course, there are some different approaches that can be taken if you wish to beat the stage consistently every time. Some include:

*Cheesing the stage by using the [[Cat Cannon]] to allow a unit to clip through CyberFace's [[Hitbox]] and destroy the base (needs timing and practice, also good Combos to have the Cannon ready).
*[[Kubiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|E. Kubilan Pasalan]] has 100% Critical Chance and Level 8 Wave Attacks. As the Wave is generated independently from its attack, it can easily catch Cyberface and destroy it instantly right after hitting the base.
*Using a [[:Category:Wave Shield Cats|Wave Shield]] with some range and many meatshields, then just taking out CyberFace one hit at a time, or using [[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|wave-immune]] attackers and meatshields directly. You can also "snipe" CyberFace's [[Wave Attack]] with a Wave Shield to ensure that your Critters don't get obliterated by timing them.
*[[:Category:Cats with Conjure ability|Units with Conjure]] can solo this stage given their base attack and Spirit deal at least 60,000 damage total. Deploy the unit, then when they are about to land their attack, activate their [[Conjure]] ability so that it hits the enemy base after Boss Shockwave pushes them back. This instantly clears the stage without needing to face the boss.
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]] can easily stall out Cyberface for a bit but not forever as Cyberface has knockback on his attacks, but the extra time can still prove vital in getting a fast rusher to steadily beat down Cyberface, be careful when sending out units besides Metal Cat before Cyberface nears the cat base with this strategy as the waves can easily render every other unit on its way dead and gone.

